## Why This Is Asked
Tests practical tenancy controls in a NoSQL store; checks how to enforce data isolation with security rules, IAM, and network boundaries; assesses ability to design automated containment.

## Key Concepts
- Firestore security rules and tenant-scoped paths
- Per-tenant service accounts with least privilege
- Private Service Connect and VPC Service Controls
- CI/CD gate with synthetic tenants and rollback

## Code Example
```javascript
// Firestore rules snippet (illustrative)
service cloud.firestore {
  match /databases/{database}/documents {
    match /tenants/{tenantId}/{document=**} {
      allow read, write: if request.auth != null && request.auth.token.tenants.contains(tenantId);
    }
  }
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you test for potential rule bypasses in CI?
- What are the trade-offs of using per-tenant collections vs single collection with tenant_id field?

## Why This Is Asked
This evaluates expertise in designing tenant-isolated logging architectures—a critical security requirement in multi-tenant SaaS platforms where log exposure can lead to data breaches.

## Key Concepts
- Cloud Logging Router with tenant-specific sinks using label-based filtering
- IAM Conditions implementing least-privilege access controls
- Data Loss Prevention API for automatic PII redaction
- CI/CD pipeline integration with synthetic tenant provisioning
- Automated rollback mechanisms for isolation verification

## Code Example
```javascript
// Conceptual tenant sink configuration
const tenantSink = {
  name: `tenant-${tenantId}-sink`,
  filter: `resource.type="cloud_run_revision" AND labels.tenant_id="${tenantId}"`,
  destination: `bigquery.googleapis.com/projects/${projectId}/datasets/tenant_${tenantId}_logs`
};

// IAM Condition for tenant access
const tenantAccessCondition = {
  title: `Tenant ${tenantId} Log Access`,
  expression: `resource.name.startsWith("projects/${projectId}/datasets/tenant_${tenantId}_")`
};
```

## Why This Is Asked
Tests practical ability to secure public Cloud Run endpoints for multiple partners using standard GCP controls.

## Key Concepts
- Least-privilege IAM per partner
- IAP for authenticating users to Cloud Run
- Per-partner isolation via separate service accounts or gateway policies
- Credential rotation and auditability
- Synthetic tests to validate misconfig denial

## Code Example
```javascript
// Pseudo test: simulate non-permitted access and expect HTTP 403
const token = obtainTokenFor('partnerX');
fetch('https://api.example.run.app/endpoint', { headers: { Authorization: `Bearer ${token}` }})
  .then(response => {
    if (response.status === 403) {
      console.log('✓ Access properly blocked for unauthorized partner');
    } else {
